dp9ik Protocol Implementation

The dp9ik authentication protocol implementation in this software includes
cryptographic code and protocol logic adapted from:

- 9front (http://9front.org/)
  9front is distributed under the Lucent Public License / MIT license

- drawterm (https://github.com/0intro/drawterm)
  drawterm's authentication code is also derived from Plan 9

The following cryptographic primitives were adapted from 9front:

- AuthPAK (src/libauthsrv/authpak.c)
- Ed448-Goldilocks elliptic curve operations (src/libauthsrv/ed448.*)
- Edwards curve operations (src/libauthsrv/edwards.*)
- Elligator2 encoding (src/libauthsrv/elligator2.*)
- SPAKE2-EE protocol (src/libauthsrv/spake2ee.*)
- Decaf point compression (src/libauthsrv/decaf.*)
- Constant-time field arithmetic (src/libmp/port/cnfield.c, gmfield.c)
- ChaCha20 stream cipher (src/libsec/port/chacha.c)
- Poly1305 MAC (src/libsec/port/poly1305.c)
- ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD (src/libsec/port/ccpoly.c)
- SHA-512 hash function (src/libsec/port/sha2_64.c)
- HKDF key derivation (src/libsec/port/hkdf.c)
- PBKDF2 key derivation (src/libsec/port/pbkdf2.c)

These components remain under the same MIT/Lucent license as Plan 9.
